From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:45:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] exp: eBPF is opt-in (ctl -a enable-ebpf / disable-ebpf)

By default the RPM now behaves like the official CloudWatch Agent: no
systemd drop-in, no extra capabilities, no eBPF config loaded.

- start-amazon-cloudwatch-agent loads etc/ebpf/obi.yaml only when the
  marker etc/ebpf/enabled exists (the old etc/ebpf/disabled is gone).
- The drop-in ships as the template etc/ebpf/systemd-dropin.conf.
  ctl -a enable-ebpf creates the marker, installs the drop-in as
  service.d/ebpf.conf and restarts (or starts) the agent;
  -a disable-ebpf removes both and restarts if running.
  ctl -a status reports "ebpf": enabled|disabled.
- Upgrades from the always-on versions keep eBPF on: %pre creates the
  marker when the old service.d/ebpf.conf exists and %posttrans
  reinstalls the drop-in before the cond-restart. A full erase removes
  the marker and the drop-in.
---
 Tools/src/create_rpm.sh                       |  4 +-
 cmd/start-amazon-cloudwatch-agent/path.go     | 33 ++++++----
 .../dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl  | 65 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.conf         |  2 +
 .../amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml         |  8 ++-
 packaging/linux/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.spec  | 31 ++++++++-
 6 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Tools/src/create_rpm.sh b/Tools/src/create_rpm.sh
